A whole shop

The group `Services` holds `Orders`, `Payments` and `Notify`. The team
`Commerce` owns `Orders` and `Payments`; the team `Growth` owns `Notify`. Use
the key `owner`. The `Web app` and the `Mobile app` call the `API gateway`. The
`API gateway` calls `Orders`. `Orders` calls `Payments`, and `Payments` calls
`Notify`. Neither app may call `Postgres`, with the reason `never directly`.
`Orders` saves to `Postgres`. Show it as a flow.
---
Services {
  Orders, Payments { owner: Commerce }
  Notify { owner: Growth }
}
Web app, Mobile app -> API gateway
API gateway -> Orders
Orders -> Payments
Payments -> Notify
Orders -> Postgres: save
Web app, Mobile app -x Postgres: never directly
show flow
